<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS entitlements for MUON.

  Today MUON ships UNSIGNED (identity: null → electron-builder ad-hoc signs the
  arm64 bundle so it launches; Gatekeeper still quarantines it → the user does
  "Open Anyway" once). These entitlements are inert without a real Developer-ID
  signature, but they are written to be correct the day notarization is flipped
  on (set APPLE_ID / APPLE_TEAM_ID / APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD + a signing
  identity, see scripts/notarize.mjs and docs/install.md).

  Why each key matters for MUON specifically:
    * allow-jit / unsigned-executable-memory , V8 (Electron + the embedded
      Node runtime) JITs; required under the hardened runtime.
    * disable-library-validation , MUON spawns the embedded backend as a child
      of the *bundled Electron binary running as Node* (ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE),
      which dlopen()s native modules NOT signed by our team: the LadybugDB
      N-API addon (lbugjs.node) and the Prisma query engine
      (libquery_engine-*.dylib.node). Without this, the hardened runtime would
      refuse to load them and the brain would fail to boot.
    * allow-dyld-environment-variables , the supervisor passes environment to
      the spawned Node child; the hardened runtime otherwise scrubs inherited
      dyld/loader environment.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
